 1.1 If $F\ne\varnothing$, use [F1] to choose an equivariant tubular disk $D_\rho(\nu_F)$ and let $K=M\setminus D_{\rho/2}(\nu_F)$, where $D_{\rho/2}$ denotes the image of the smaller open disk. This is closed in compact $M$, hence compact by [F6]. Every $x\in K$ is nonfixed, so its stabilizer $H_x\subsetneq T$ is a proper closed subgroup. If $F=\varnothing$, set $K=M$; it is compact and every point is nonfixed. If $F=M$, then $K=\varnothing$. For each $x\in K$, [F1] gives an open invariant orbit tube $V_x$ with all stabilizers contained in $H_x$; compactness gives a finite subcover $V_1,\ldots,V_m$ of $K$. For $F\ne\varnothing$, the sphere bundle $Q=S_{\rho/2}(\nu_F)\subset K$ is compact: cover the compact base by finitely many relatively compact bundle charts; over each compact chart closure the sphere fiber is compact, and the finitely many resulting compact sets cover $Q$. [A1, F1, F6, given, construct]
 
-2.1 Consider any invariant open set $W\subseteq V_j\cong T\times_{H_j}D(V_j^0)$. Its inverse image in the slice has the form $T\times_{H_j}W_0$ for an $H_j$-invariant open $W_0\subseteq D(V_j^0)$. The Borel identification is the homeomorphism $[e,[t,w]]\mapsto[e\cdot t,w]$ from $ET\times_T(T\times_{H_j}W_0)$ to $ET\times_{H_j}W_0$, with inverse $[e,w]\mapsto[e,[1,w]]$; the quotient relations show both maps are well-defined. Write $B_H=ET/H$. The map $B_H\to BT$ is the associated quotient bundle $ET\times_T(T/H)\to BT$, and [F4] gives its compact-fiber CW-type and paracompactness properties. Since $ET\to BT$ is numerable, this associated quotient bundle is numerable as well: its local product charts over each Milnor chart retain the same subordinate partition. By [F4], $ET\to B_H$ is locally a principal $H$-bundle: over a Milnor $T$-chart it has form $U\times T\to U\times(T/H)$, and local sections of the Lie quotient $T\to T/H$ give the principal $H$-charts. The projection $q:B_H\to BT$ pulls $L_\chi$ back to the associated line $ET\times_H\mathbb C_{\chi|_H}$; the explicit trivialization $[e,z]\mapsto([e]_H,z)$ is well-defined because $\chi|_H=1$. Thus this is a numerable trivial line bundle, using its global chart and the constant partition $1$. The space $B_H$ is path-connected as a continuous image of contractible $ET$, so [F5] applies and its first Chern class is zero. Under the Borel identification, the projection $ET\times_H W_0\to BT$ factors through $B_H$, and the character class on $ET\times_H W_0$ is the pullback of this zero class. It therefore acts as zero on $H_T^*(W;k)$. As $\chi$ is nontrivial, this class becomes invertible in $\mathscr S_T(k)$, and the localized module is zero. [F2, F3, F4, F5, given, construct]
