-3.1 Let $W_j\subseteq V_j$ be any finite family of invariant open subsets, with each $V_j$ an orbit tube as above. We prove $\mathscr S_T(k)^{-1}H_T^*(\bigcup_{j=1}^m W_j;k)=0$ by induction on $m$. It holds for $m=1$ by step 2.1. For $m>1$, put $A=\bigcup_{j<m}W_j$ and $B=W_m$. By induction the localized cohomology of $A$ is zero, and step 2.1 gives zero for $B$. The intersection $A\cap B\subseteq V_m$ is invariant and open, so step 2.1 also gives zero for it. The Borel quotients of invariant open sets are open, since the quotient map is open (the saturation of an open set is the union of its $T$-translates). Thus Mayer–Vietoris applies to the Borel open cover. To see that localization preserves its long exactness, split the sequence at each image/kernel into short exact module sequences and apply [F8] to each; exactness of the localized pieces then gives exactness at every Mayer–Vietoris term. The segment from the localized $H^q(A\cap B;k)$ through $H^{q+1}(A\cup B;k)$ to the localized $H^{q+1}(A;k)\oplus H^{q+1}(B;k)$ has zero end terms, forcing the middle term to vanish in every degree. [F8, step 2.1, induction, algebra]
